{
  "description": "Which knowledge-base collections one account may search. 'rows' are the llm_knowledgebases rows a query returns before this rule runs: not archived, integration enabled, and either owned by the querying account or in its tenant (kb.tenant_id = the account's tenant). A row with account_id null is an organisation knowledge base; override_enabled is the querying account's switch for it (null = none). Rules: another account's manual KB is never visible; the account's own manual KB shadows an organisation KB whose non-empty name matches after lowercasing (Python str.lower / Go strings.ToLower, not Unicode case folding) (even while switched off); integration KBs keep their per-account switch. 'account': null is a tenant-only query (no account resolved). Collections: kb_<id> for manual rows, <integration_id>_knowledge_base for integration rows.",
